{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SNvZiL5VdV5Nn4irecCZa2","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# AMERICAN FOOTBALL FIASCO\n11:## 0. Read this first\n13:### 0.1 The title\n18:### 0.2 Names and deliverables\n28:### 0.3 Working rules (from TASK.md, repeated here so none is missed)\n45:### 0.4 How to read this plan\n56:## 1. The game on one page\n90:## 2. TASK.md coverage map\n132:## 3. Tech stack and setup\n134:### 3.1 What you build on\n154:### 3.2 Fetching (sparse, into your dev folder)\n170:### 3.3 The dev folder\n197:### 3.4 The dev page\n203:### 3.5 The bundle (`node build.mjs`)\n214:### 3.6 Engine changes to make (log each in ENGINE-CHANGES.md)\n234:## 4. Architecture\n236:### 4.1 Principles\n258:### 4.2 Namespace and file pattern\n264:### 4.3 Modules (load order)\n312:### 4.4 Scenes and the flow between them\n325:### 4.5 One step of a match (`match.update(dt)`)\n341:### 4.6 The `game.debug` handle (for tests and tools)\n357:## 5. World, units and the stadium\n359:### 5.1 Units\n364:### 5.2 Field geometry\n384:### 5.3 The TileMap\n400:### 5.4 Floor painting (`floorTex(x, y, tag)`)\n413:### 5.5 Dressing per stadium\n420:### 5.6 Views\n436:## 6. Football rules and the match flow (`30-sim.js`)\n438:### 6.1 The match state machine\n470:### 6.2 Downs, distance and spotting\n479:### 6.3 Scoring\n489:### 6.4 Kicks\n500:### 6.5 The clock\n510:### 6.6 Turnovers and possession changes\n520:## 7. Athletes, movement and actions\n522:### 7.1 Ratings\n528:### 7.2 Movement\n543:### 7.3 Collisions between athletes\n552:### 7.4 The action system\n578:### 7.5 Tackle resolution\n596:### 7.6 The ball (`28-ball.js`)\n623:### 7.7 Catches, interceptions, deflections, fumbles and pile-ups\n648:### 7.8 Kicking and the kick meter\n664:### 7.9 Blocking\n680:## 8. The AI (`33-ai.js`, `34-ai-coach.js`)\n682:### 8.1 Brains and behaviors\n717:### 8.2 Play assignments (data to brain)\n730:### 8.3 Special teams brains\n734:### 8.4 Difficulty\n745:### 8.5 The coach AI (play calling, cards, decisions)\n764:### 8.6 The Play Lab (an AI quality tool and test)\n780:## 9. Controls and human control (`35-control.js`)\n782:### 9.1 The input map (`FF.KEYS`)\n806:### 9.2 The control table by context\n846:### 9.3 Prompts that follow the device\n866:### 9.4 Who controls whom\n885:### 9.5 The mouse on the field\n897:## 10. The over-the-top systems (`36-ots.js`)\n899:### 10.1 Hot Streak (\"BLAZING!\")\n915:### 10.2 The Fiasco Meter and the Fiasco Cards (the items)\n952:### 10.3 Big Hits, Mega Hits, Dinged and the flying helmet\n965:### 10.4 Late hits\n970:### 10.5 Boss specials (story bosses; also in exhibition)\n986:### 10.6 Celebrations\n1004:### 10.7 Mascots\n1010:### 10.8 Refs\n1017:### 10.9 LIGHTS OUT (chapter 3's event; also a Dev toggle)\n1025:## 11. Presentation\n1027:### 11.1 The camera director (`37-camera.js`)\n1046:### 11.2 Instant replay and the highlight reel (`38-replay.js`)\n1066:### 11.3 Commentary and on-field text (`39-commentary.js`)\n1087:### 11.4 The crowd (`26-crowd.js`)\n1100:### 11.5 FX (`40-fx.js`)\n1127:## 12. Art and animation\n1129:### 12.1 The look target (from API.md: use every step)\n1136:### 12.2 Characters (`27-rigs.js`)\n1178:### 12.3 Pose codes to animation (`FF.Rigs.drive(rig, athlete, dt)`)\n1218:### 12.4 Motion clips (the FIASCO set)\n1237:### 12.5 PoseFX (new animation by joint post-processing)\n1248:### 12.6 New shapes (`24-shapes.js`) and store props\n1279:### 12.7 The football\n1287:### 12.8 Logos, field art and UI art\n1305:### 12.9 Checking the art\n1312:## 13. Audio (`20-audio-voice.js`, `21-audio-music.js`)\n1317:### 13.1 Music (`{ bpm, steps, tracks }`, named tracks for layers)\n1338:### 13.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` each; the engine warns on unknown names, and a test fails on such a warning)\n1348:### 13.3 The crowd bed\n1355:### 13.4 Voices: the babble synth (Animalese and Simlish)\n1411:## 14. Screens and UX (10-foot, controller-first)\n1413:### 14.1 Rules for every screen\n1433:### 14.2 Title\n1441:### 14.3 Main menu\n1447:### 14.4 Exhibition setup (two steps)\n1458:### 14.5 The play-call screen (`53-playcall.js`)\n1475:### 14.6 The HUD (`41-hud.js`)\n1488:### 14.7 The kick meter\n1495:### 14.8 Results\n1502:### 14.9 Hall of Fiasco (records)\n1508:### 14.10 About & Credits\n1521:### 14.11 Settings\n1531:### 14.12 Touch-only devices\n1543:### 14.13 The pause menu\n1552:## 15. Modes\n1554:### 15.1 Story: THE FIASCO CUP (`54-scene-story.js`, `14-data-story.js`)\n1596:### 15.2 Tutorial and practice drills (`55-scene-drills.js`, `15-data-drills.js`)\n1614:### 15.3 Exhibition\n1618:### 15.4 The attract mode (`56-scene-attract.js`, `17-data-attract.js`)\n1652:## 16. Multiplayer (`80-net.js`)\n1654:### 16.1 How TASK.md's multiplayer line is met\n1662:### 16.2 The page head\n1677:### 16.3 A session, step by step (when `AIHub.active`)\n1703:### 16.4 Roles\n1712:### 16.5 Messages, rates, prediction (formats in Appendix B)\n1740:### 16.6 Session rules (the protocol's, and what they mean here)\n1755:### 16.7 Results\n1764:## 17. Dev mode (`70-dev.js`)\n1806:## 18. Content\n1808:### 18.1 Teams and rosters (`10-data-teams.js`)\n1970:### 18.2 Stadiums (`12-data-stadiums.js`)\n1983:### 18.3 Plays (`11-data-plays.js`; coordinates in yards from the ball spot, x downfield, y + to the offense's right)\n2051:### 18.4 Fiasco Cards\n2055:### 18.5 Commentary line banks (`16-data-lines.js`)\n2093:### 18.6 The story scripts (`14-data-story.js`; [stage directions] become E.Story `event` steps)\n2220:## 19. Build order and milestones\n2240:## 20. Risks and how to de-risk them\n2261:## 21. Testing\n2263:### 21.1 The one command\n2276:### 21.2 The suites\n2296:### 21.3 Devices in tests\n2303:### 21.4 Determinism\n2307:### 21.5 Filmstrips (animation review; not in the one command)\n2312:### 21.6 Screenshots (only for what a script can't judge)\n2325:## 22. Tuning defaults (the Dev sliders; `02-tuning.js`)\n2338:### 22.2 Balance targets\n2357:## 23. Definition of done an