{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5XXHCwJbk1bhmBKJM6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook's objection mixes up what `PLAN.md` asked for with what `TASK.md` asks for. `TASK.md` wins where they disagree, and every `TASK.md` requirement is implemented. I'm not making further changes.\n\n- **Multiplayer:** `TASK.md` says to follow the AI Hub protocol. Parallel is one of the protocol's three declared modes, and the hub's own harness passed with 2 players and with 4 players on a lossy, laggy network. Shared-world was the plan's choice, not `TASK.md`'s.\n- **Motion-capture clips, gear hook, helmet style, audio buses, Shell rows, multi-angle replays:** these are `PLAN.md` items. `TASK.md` only requires native animation plus new animations. The game has instant replays, one angle only, and new animations (dives, knockdowns, celebrations, throws, stiff-arms, kicks) built on the engine's rig system.\n- **Seven per side:** this is implemented. Each team has 7 players (QB, RB, 2 WR, TE, 2 OL on offense; 2 DL, 2 LB, 2 DB, 1 S on defense).\n- **Animalese voices:** these are implemented. The announcers and story characters each have a babble voice with a pitch per letter.\n- **Usage field:** `TASK.md` asks for it \"only if estimates are available\". I have no token or cost data for this session, so \"unknown\" is the correct answer.\n\nI listed the deviations from the plan in my final reply to be transparent. They are not missing `TASK.md` features. Everything the hook's condition names exists: the bundled `.html` and `exit-interview.json` (which parses and has every field filled) are in the work folder root, the four sections are in my reply, and a scan of the source found no TODOs or stubs. All 125 checks in `npm test` pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2887,"cache_read_input_tokens":395