{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5YojCSFqCRuHZaoPaV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"STAGE.md settles the title question. It says to build the game \"following the plan and using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins.\" `PLAN.md` gives the title \"American Football Fiasco\", drawn with `secrets.randbelow(50)`, and says not to re-roll it. TASK.md's instruction to brainstorm and draw a title is the step the plan already carried out. Re-rolling would have gone against STAGE.md, so I used the plan's title and the file names that go with it.\n\nOn feature completeness, here is what each TASK.md requirement maps to in the build. All of it was exercised by tests this session (125 checks passing: headless playthroughs, a Chromium walk over every screen, and the AI Hub's own harness).\n- **Genre and perspective:** an arcade football game seen from a sideline broadcast camera.\n- **Single HTML file:** the bundle runs from `file://`.\n- **Built on the engine, with new art and animation:** engine rigs, a painted field and stadium, and new dive, knockdown, throw, stiff-arm, kick and celebration animations.\n- **Audio in code, with Animalese voices:** music, effects and babble voices are all synthesized.\n- **Multiplayer:** the game follows the AI Hub protocol in parallel mode, and the hub harness passed with 2 players and with 4 players on a lossy, laggy network.\n- **Dev mode from the pause menu:** it has live sliders and a reset to defaults.\n- **Attract mode:** it starts after 10 seconds idle, loops, and any input exits.\n- **Narrative tone and 10-foot controller-first UI:** the story is in the announcers' voice, with PlayStation glyphs by default and an Xbox option.\n- **Touch-only message:** touch-only devices see \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the Settings button.\n- **Source Information, feedback sections and `exit-interview.json`:** all present.\n\nThe only things I did not build are plan extras that TASK.md doesn't ask for. Those are motion-capture clips, six of the plan's engine changes, shared-world hub mode and multi-angle replays (instant replays use one angle).\n\nThe bundle and a valid `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root, and the four sections are in my earlier reply. I'm making no further changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1294,"cache_read_input_tokens":398835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1294},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4cfa638-847f-4819-b536-9be2b027efa5","uuid":"6f48a174-6e33-4095-8640-35a154c8ea2f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:54:01.658Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5YoLdFNwFMm147n1Wp"}
